Timothy Grove. Advanced Igneous Petrology, MIT 12.490, Fall 2005, graduate level. [Official course, syllabus, readings, labs, and study material](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/12-490-advanced-igneous-petrology-fall-2005/).

Complete the published sequence during advanced igneous work, reading the original papers assigned to the case studies where authorized access is available. Compare experimental constraints, mineral chemistry, textures, and geological histories across the selected natural systems. Published teaching studies do not themselves supply all laboratory access or complete campus assessment.

MIT OCW and individual third-party notices apply; commercial or restricted papers remain separately accessed sources. Course identity, level, instructor, year, and public material categories checked on 29 October 2026. Distinguish the historical course literature from later revisions and research. Reference only, with no course media/data collection in the repository.

